ation", "Reproductive-age woman (23) who is sexually active without condoms", "Urinary β-hCG test ordered (implicating concern for ectopic pregnancy)"], "excluded_candidates": ["Ovarian cyst torsion: Less likely than ruptured ectopic pregnancy given hypotension and β-hCG context", "Acute cholecystitis: Unlikely to fully explain hypovolemic shock pattern", "Alcohol-induced acute pancreatitis: Notable for RULQ pain but lacks key lab evidence", "Exercise-associated rhabdomyolysis: Could cause pain but would not produce hypotension"], "alarm_features": ["Severe hypotension with tachycardia (hemodynamic instability)", "Acute surgical abdomen suspicion with intra-abdominal hemorrhage concern", "Unidentified acute gynecological pathology (pending β-hCG results)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Acute Gynecological Emergency", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.4948453608247424, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The abrupt hemodynamic derangement (B1/B5) is more consistent with acute hemorrhage than gradual hepatic ischemia, strongly excluding inflammatory/vascular mec…"], "evidence_against": ["RUQ pain does not strongly exclude gynecological cause (B1) since ectopic rupture can present atypically. However, it provides weak support for biliary (B2) an…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.85, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Biliary Tract Emergency", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.165, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The abrupt hemodynamic derangement (B1/B5) is more consistent with acute hemorrhage than gradual hepatic ischemia, strongly excluding inflammatory/vascular mec…"]}, "B3": {"id": "B